                <pb facs="0803" n="795" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2224: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-28T19:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>326. Paragraph numbered 2 of your 756, August 27, 6 p.m. Please seek an early
                    occasion to inform Mr. Matsuoka that so far as this Government is aware there
                    was no intrigue and no understanding with regard to the question of the disposal
                    to be made of the sectors formerly allocated in the defense plan to the British
                    forces and that we were given by the British very short notice of their
                    intention to withdraw their forces from their sectors.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
